-- Mickey's Not-So-Scary Halloween Party (MNSSHP) 2026: 7 new Kiosk booths
-- and 59 Snack & Sip items at Magic Kingdom, mirroring the EPCOT Food & Wine
-- kiosk/booth pattern (category 'kiosk' for booths, category 'snack' with
-- booth_id for items, seasonal jsonb for the date range).
--
-- Ticket gating: unlike Food & Wine, MNSSHP is a separate hard-ticket event,
-- so seasonal carries ticket_required: true. The source spreadsheet notes
-- that the party only runs select nights within Aug 7 - Oct 31 (not every
-- night) -- that finer-grained party calendar isn't captured here; seasonal
-- start/end mark the outer season only, same limitation as the F&W booths.
--
-- Party Only / Day & Party / Day Only availability (MNSSHP has all three,
-- where F&W items are always festival-only) is stored as a tags entry
-- alongside 'New 2026' and 'Plant-based', following the existing
-- free-form-tags convention rather than adding a dedicated column.
--
-- Closing times ("Party Closes At" in the source) are folded into the
-- Kiosk booth description text rather than a new schema column, matching
-- how F&W booth hours/logistics live in prose today.
--
-- 12 of the 19 locations already existed in the catalog (regular MK dining/
-- snack rows) and are merged into their existing ids via booth_id rather
-- than duplicated -- same pattern as the regular snacks catalog import.
-- Only the 7 missing locations (Plaza Ice Cream Parlor, Auntie Gravity's,
-- Cheshire Cafe, Storybook Treats, Friar's Nook, Liberty Square Market,
-- Aloha Isle Refreshments) get new kiosk-mn-* rows.
--
-- Prices came from a follow-up version of the source spreadsheet with a
-- Price column added; price_label is formatted '~$X.XX' to match the
-- existing snack catalog convention. The Be Our Guest and Cinderella's
-- Royal Table party items share one flat per-person price across their
-- multiple courses/drinks (a prix-fixe menu), not per-item pricing --
-- that's the real structure of those party menus, not a data error.
--
-- Queen of Hearts Tart is Day Only at Cheshire Cafe and Party Only at
-- Storybook Treats -- same item name, two different locations/states, so
-- the Storybook Treats row gets a disambiguated id.
on conflict (id) do update set name=excluded.name, park=excluded.park, category=excluded.category, description=excluded.description, price_label=excluded.price_label, price_mid=excluded.price_mid, location_detail=excluded.location_detail, dining_tier=excluded.dining_tier, cuisine=excluded.cuisine, dining_plan_credits=excluded.dining_plan_credits, seasonal=excluded.seasonal, tags=excluded.tags, booth_id=excluded.booth_id, item_type=excluded.item_type;
